# Real crash-reopen consistency test on the emitted core.db engine:
# crashes every reachable write, truncate, delete, and sync boundary of a
# multi-page two-transaction workload (both rollback-journal DELETE and WAL
# modes, including dropped and seeded reordered unsynced writes), verifies
# PRAGMA integrity_check = ok and whole-or-absent transactions on every reopen,
# and proves a real failing schedule under synchronous = OFF replays from its
# seed and reduces to a minimal counterexample.
fixture: CrashReopen.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet test main.jet --filter db_crash_reopen
exit: 0
stdout: ~ "db_crash_reopen: pass" # db_crash_reopen passes across every reachable write/sync boundary
